## Five-bucket disjoint-set matrix (this report's contribution)

The payload above carries the per-bucket lists but does not enumerate them
as **disjoint, invariant-checked sets** in a committed artifact. This report
closes that gap. The buckets are now defined as follows (committed in
`v2/backend/app/services/symbol_universe/coverage_buckets.py`):

| bucket          | semantic                                                                                    | population source                                                                              | safety invariant                                                                                          |
|-----------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `DISCOVERED`    | known by any source feed (CoinAnk ODT, Binance USDM, KuCoin, CoinAPI, future ingestors)      | union of source adapters                                                                       | none — pure observation                                                                                   |
| `OBSERVED`      | discovered ∧ has live `v2:market:*` freshness proof within freshness window                  | runtime ingestor heartbeats                                                                    | `OBSERVED ⊆ DISCOVERED`                                                                                   |
| `TRAINING`      | operator-approved subset eligible for trainer enrollment                                      | explicit operator allowlist (Symbol Universe governance gate)                                  | `TRAINING ⊆ OBSERVED`; `TRAINING ≠ DISCOVERED` unless explicit `FORCE_TRAIN_ALL` override                  |
| `PAPER`         | operator-approved subset eligible for paper trading                                           | explicit operator allowlist (Symbol Universe governance gate)                                  | `PAPER ⊆ OBSERVED`; `PAPER ≠ DISCOVERED` unless explicit `FORCE_PAPER_ALL` override                        |
| `LIVE_BLOCKED`  | every symbol the system knows about — live execution is default-deny                          | `DISCOVERED ∪ TRAINING ∪ PAPER`                                                                | `LIVE_BLOCKED ⊇ DISCOVERED`; `live_symbols == []` while `live_gate == blocked_human_only`                  |

`TRAINING` and `PAPER` are **not** derived automatically from `OBSERVED`; they are
operator-allowlisted via the Symbol Universe governance gate
(`v2/backend/app/services/symbol_universe/service.py::apply_manual_override`).
Auto-enrollment of all discovered symbols is rejected by the invariant checker.

## Per-source feed validation

Source enumeration: `service.py::DYNAMIC_SYMBOL_SOURCES` and adapters under
`v2/backend/app/adapters/symbol_sources/`. Each source is validated against the
director's `DATA_SOURCE_VALIDATION_MATRIX.json` (2026-05-31).

